   "answerText": "53.7",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1.5455,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p><img src=\"media/92/9237bd0edaed52af5901.png\" alt=\"\" /></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: .25in; text-align: justify;\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: 'Yu Gothic'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;\">Since unit of Mbps is not mentioned in question, therefore one can take 1 Mbps = 2^20 bits/second. So, Line speed = 53739520/2^20 = 51.25 Mbps. After round to one decimal place answer is 51.2 Mbps. But we suggest every student to take units according to SI unit standard when it is not specified in the question. So that they always has chance to proof that this is standard.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></strong></p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Ref. link. </strong><strong>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data-rate_units<br /></strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src=\"media/71/71d7dfffad0b9a0eff17.png\" alt=\"\" /></p>\n<p></p>",
   "marksApprox": true
